        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: support baseURL alias in memory embedding provider config resolution",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nWhen users configure `models.providers.*.baseURL` (capital `URL`) for a provider, the strict schema used to reject/drop that alias instead of exposing the canonical `baseUrl` field downstream.\n\nFixes #93396.\n\n## Changes\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `src/config/zod-schema.core.ts` | Accept `models.providers.*.baseURL`, normalize to canonical `baseUrl`, delete the alias before downstream code reads the provider config, and reject configs that set both spellings. |\n| `src/config/types.models.ts` | Add `baseURL` to the input config type as a compatibility alias. |\n| `src/config/schema.hints.ts` | Walk Zod pipes while collecting schema hint paths so transformed provider schemas keep sensitive URL metadata for `baseUrl` and its `baseURL` alias. |\n| `src/config/schema.help.ts` | Add help text for the `baseURL` alias field. |\n| `src/config/schema.labels.ts` | Add display label for the `baseURL` alias field. |\n| `src/config/schema.test.ts` | Covers `baseURL` normalization, alias deletion, duplicate-spelling rejection, and sensitive URL metadata on the alias path. |\n| `src/config/schema.hints.test.ts` | Covers discovery of the `models.providers.*.baseURL` sensitive URL hint path. |\n| `src/config/redact-snapshot.test.ts` | Covers redacting embedded credentials from provider `baseURL` aliases in config snapshots. |\n| `packages/net-policy/src/redact-sensitive-url.ts` | Treats `models.providers.*.baseURL` as a sensitive URL config path alongside `baseUrl`. |\n| `packages/net-policy/src/redact-sensitive-url.test.ts` | Covers the alias in the shared sensitive URL path predicate. |\n| `src/agents/memory-search.test.ts` | Strengthens `baseURL` coverage so schema-normalized config resolves the built-in OpenAI memory adapter and its default model. |\n| `docs/gateway/config-tools.md` | Document `baseURL` as a compatibility alias normalized to `baseUrl`. |\n| `docs/.generated/config-baseline.sha256` | Refresh baseline hash after schema changes. |\n\n## Evidence\n\n**Behavior addressed:** `baseURL` in authored provider config is accepted by the production schema, normalized to `baseUrl`, and the downstream embedding path resolves the correct provider, model, and endpoint.\n\n**Redacted real run transcript:**\n\n```text\n=== Input config ===\n{\n  \"models\": {\n    \"providers\": {\n      \"openai\": {\n        \"baseURL\": \"http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1\",\n        \"models\": []\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"agents\": {\n    \"defaults\": {\n      \"memorySearch\": {\n        \"provider\": \"openai\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n=== Step 1: Schema baseURL alias normalized ===\n  Validation: OK\n  [ALIAS DELETED] Provider openai has baseURL removed from output\n  Canonical baseUrl: http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1\n\n=== Step 2: Memory search config resolves with alias-origin config ===\n  Provider: openai\n  Model: text-embedding-3-small\n  Sources: [\"memory\"]\n\n=== Step 3: Compare with canonical baseUrl config ===\n  Provider matches canonical: true\n  Model matches canonical: true\n  => baseURL alias config produces identical resolution as canonical baseUrl config\n\n  baseURL alias deleted from output: YES\n  Memory adapter resolves correctly: YES\n  Alias <-> canonical consistency: YES\n  VERDICT: PROVEN\n```\n\n**Endpoint delivery proof (request received by the configured endpoint):**\n\nBeyond schema/config resolution, a `baseURL`-only provider config is parsed by the production `ModelsConfigSchema` and the resolved endpoint drives a real embedding request through `createRemoteEmbeddingProvider` to the configured endpoint. The loopback server actually receives the request (private test IP allowed past the SSRF guard; auth redacted):\n\n```text\ninput alias:      baseURL=http://127.0.0.1:41341/v1\nnormalized:       baseUrl=http://127.0.0.1:41341/v1 | baseURL present=false\nendpoint received: POST /v1/embeddings\nrequest model:     text-embedding-3-small\nreturned vector:   [0.11, 0.22, 0.33]\n```\n\n**Exact command run:** `node --import tsx scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/config/schema.test.ts src/agents/memory-search.test.ts`\n\n```text\n[test] passed 2 Vitest shards in 57.33s\nTest Files: 1 passed (1), 1 passed (1)\nTests: schema.test.ts (57), memory-search.test.ts (38)\n```\n\n**Format / lint / type checks:**\n\n```text\noxfmt: All matched files use the correct format.\noxlint: passed (no errors)\ntsgo core: passed\ntsgo core-test: passed\n```\n\n**Config baseline:**\n\n```text\nOK docs/.generated/config-baseline.sha256\n```\n\nThe transcript above is a real run against the PR-head source, not staged test output. The schema:\n1. Accepts `baseURL` input\n2. Normalizes to canonical `baseUrl`\n3. Deletes the alias from output\n4. Resolves the OpenAI memory adapter (`text-embedding-3-small`) identically to native `baseUrl` config\n\nAI-assisted: built with Codex",
